  "solution": {
    "text": "For a balanced meter bridge,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)&#215;&#8203;</mo><mn>39.5</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>39.5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12.5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>39.5</mn></mrow><mn>60.5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8.16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. When <math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;and&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi></math> are interchanged <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>l</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mn>100</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub> <mi>l</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> will also interchange,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>60.</mn><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />&nbsp;",
